#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson describes reference states, the initialization of a quantum state prior to any variational parameters."
msgstr "Pelajaran ini menjelaskan reference state, yaitu inisialisasi state kuantum sebelum parameter variasional apa pun diterapkan."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference states"
msgstr "Reference state"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will explore how we can initialize our system with a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The initial, fixed start for our problem. Typically this refers to |0>, but we can configure it to a variety of states that suitably encode our problem.\">reference state</DefinitionTooltip> to help our variational algorithm converge faster. First, we will learn how to construct a reference state manually, and then explore several standard options that can be used in a variational algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan mengeksplorasi bagaimana kita bisa menginisialisasi sistem kita dengan sebuah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Titik awal tetap awal untuk masalah kita. Biasanya ini mengacu pada |0>, tetapi kita bisa mengkonfigurasinya ke berbagai state yang sesuai untuk mengkodekan masalah kita.\">reference state</DefinitionTooltip> untuk membantu algoritma variasional kita konvergen lebih cepat. Pertama, kita akan belajar cara membuat reference state secara manual, kemudian mengeksplorasi beberapa opsi standar yang bisa digunakan dalam algoritma variasional.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Diagram of options for references states including default, application-specific, and quantum.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states/reference-workflow.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Diagram opsi untuk reference state termasuk default, spesifik-aplikasi, dan kuantum.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states/reference-workflow.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default state {#default-state}"
msgstr "State default {#default-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A *reference state* refers to the initial fixed start for our problem. To prepare a reference state, we need to apply the appropriate, non-parametrized unitary $U_R$ at the start of our quantum circuit, such that $|\\rho\\rangle = U_R |0\\rangle$. If you have an educated guess or datapoint from an existing optimal solution, the variational algorithm will likely converge faster if you use that as a starting point.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah *reference state* mengacu pada titik awal tetap awal untuk masalah kita. Untuk mempersiapkan reference state, kita perlu menerapkan uniter $U_R$ yang sesuai dan non-terparameter di awal Circuit kuantum kita, sehingga $|\\rho\\rangle = U_R |0\\rangle$. Jika kamu memiliki tebakan atau data dari solusi optimal yang sudah ada, algoritma variasional kemungkinan besar akan konvergen lebih cepat jika kamu menggunakannya sebagai titik awal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest possible reference state is the default state, where we use the starting state of an $n$-qubit quantum circuit: $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$. For the default state, our unitary operator $U_R \\equiv I$. Due to its simplicity, the default state is a valid reference state used in many scenarios.\n"
msgstr "Reference state paling sederhana adalah state default, di mana kita menggunakan state awal dari Circuit kuantum $n$-Qubit: $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$. Untuk state default, operator uniter kita $U_R \\equiv I$. Karena kesederhanaannya, state default adalah reference state yang valid dan digunakan dalam banyak skenario.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical reference state {#classical-reference-state}"
msgstr "Reference state klasik {#classical-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose you have a three-qubit system and you want to start in the state $|001\\rangle$ instead of the default state $|000\\rangle$. This is an example of a purely classical reference state, and to construct it, you simply need to apply an [X gate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) to qubit $0$ (following Qiskit's qubit ordering), as $|001\\rangle = X_0 |000\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Misalkan kamu memiliki sistem tiga-Qubit dan ingin memulai dalam state $|001\\rangle$ alih-alih state default $|000\\rangle$. Ini adalah contoh reference state murni klasik, dan untuk membuatnya, kamu cukup menerapkan [Gate X](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) ke qubit $0$ (mengikuti pengurutan qubit Qiskit), karena $|001\\rangle = X_0 |000\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this case, our unitary operator is $U_R \\equiv X_0$, which leads to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle \\equiv |001\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kasus ini, operator uniter kita adalah $U_R \\equiv X_0$, yang menghasilkan reference state $|\\rho\\rangle \\equiv |001\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states/extracted-outputs/cfd71225-1f9f-4a34-b825-ae19813956a8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/reference-states/extracted-outputs/cfd71225-1f9f-4a34-b825-ae19813956a8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum reference state {#quantum-reference-state}"
msgstr "Reference state kuantum {#quantum-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose you aim to start with a more complex state that involves superposition and/or entanglement, such as $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|100\\rangle+|111\\rangle)$.\n"
msgstr "Misalkan kamu bertujuan untuk memulai dengan state yang lebih kompleks yang melibatkan superposisi dan/atau entanglement, seperti $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|100\\rangle+|111\\rangle)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To obtain this state from $|000\\rangle$, one approach is to use a [Hadamard gate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.HGate) on qubit $0$ ($H_0$), a [CNOT (CX)](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CXGate) gate with qubit $0$ as the control qubit and qubit $1$ as the target qubit ($CNOT_{01}$), and finally an $X$ gate applied to qubit $2$ ($X_2$).\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapatkan state ini dari $|000\\rangle$, salah satu pendekatannya adalah menggunakan [Gate Hadamard](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.HGate) pada qubit $0$ ($H_0$), sebuah Gate [CNOT (CX)](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CXGate) dengan qubit $0$ sebagai qubit kontrol dan qubit $1$ sebagai qubit target ($CNOT_{01}$), dan akhirnya Gate $X$ yang diterapkan ke qubit $2$ ($X_2$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this scenario, our unitary operator is $U_{R} \\equiv X_2CNOT_{01}H_0|000\\rangle$, and our reference state is $|\\rho\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|100\\rangle+|111\\rangle)$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam skenario ini, operator uniter kita adalah $U_{R} \\equiv X_2CNOT_{01}H_0|000\\rangle$, dan reference state kita adalah $|\\rho\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|100\\rangle+|111\\rangle)$.\n"

